{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01M1:prose-0001", "parent_tag": "01M1", "chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent sheaf of <MATH_0003>-modules.\nBy Modules, Lemma <REF_0001>\nthe symmetric algebra <MATH_0004> of\n<MATH_0005> over <MATH_0006>\nis a quasi-coherent sheaf of <MATH_0007>-algebras.\nHence it makes sense to apply the relative spectrum.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{modules-lemma-whole-tensor-algebra-permanence}", "MATH_0004": "$\\text{Sym}(\\mathcal{E})$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:7f16e1f2612a666be627c98fc0189ac13f8aed6bcc506f86a9111dbddb6315f2", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:53ecbea4f5355396ef2404dfdbd37373a255be43559db52db247c6be21d9fdbb", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6dbbcfa0b9eda0b2a622f9fefc5b354f875582e1e64b7d3f8cb94b78a65bd391"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01M2:statement", "parent_tag": "01M1", "chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "definition", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent\n<MATH_0003>-module<FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>The reader may expect here\nthe condition that <MATH_0004> is finite locally free. We do not\ndo so in order to be consistent with <REF_0001>.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001>.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>vector bundle associated to <MATH_0005><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is\n<MATH_0006>\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "REF_0001": "\\cite[II, Definition 1.7.8]{EGA}", "FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\mathbf{V}(\\mathcal{E}) = \\underline{\\Spec}_S(\\text{Sym}(\\mathcal{E})).\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-vector-bundle}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:60168c6c1b891120fee146c507238647155e122a429e25f590ac4cb13508d5a4", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6df7b759e79563346bc891ef7660ff97c8bebd8769b78ea9998674733d5c5478", "source_math_hash": "sha256:61fc6bf3eace60e53f2fbfe63f377cef68de9637bfec3b420df4da49540d0bed"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01M1:prose-0002", "parent_tag": "01M1", "chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe vector bundle associated to <MATH_0001> comes with a bit\nof extra structure. Namely, we have a grading\n<MATH_0002>\nwhich turns <MATH_0003>\ninto a graded <MATH_0004>-algebra. Conversely, we can recover\n<MATH_0005> from the degree <MATH_0006> part of this.\nThus we define an abstract vector bundle as follows.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\pi_*\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathbf{V}(\\mathcal{E})} =\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{n \\geq 0} \\text{Sym}^n(\\mathcal{E}).\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$\\pi_*\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathbf{V}(\\mathcal{E})}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0006": "$1$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:e5cfa2dd33a002cdae0f4fbcf0a89e11a16371c554de9597ece29681e8e10851", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6cc7447d4078d3a7e6c032ba1bc083d169837e9a374a4078d024cc75ea07ef54", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a0329ea18813d34eaecdc8a8edbea5f0eb969cc5adb386a7eff35e4064be8722"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:062M:statement", "parent_tag": "01M1", "chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "definition", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>vector bundle <MATH_0002> over <MATH_0003><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is an\naffine morphism of schemes such that <MATH_0004> is endowed with\nthe structure of a graded <MATH_0005>-algebra\n<MATH_0006>\nsuch that <MATH_0007> and such that the maps\n<MATH_0008>\nare isomorphisms for all <MATH_0009>. A <TEXTITOPEN_0002>morphism of vector bundles\nover <MATH_0010><TEXTITCLOSE_0002> is a morphism <MATH_0011> such that the induced map\n<MATH_0012>\nis compatible with the given gradings.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "MATH_0002": "$\\pi : V \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "MATH_0004": "$\\pi_*\\mathcal{O}_V$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0006": "$\\pi_*\\mathcal{O}_V = \\bigoplus\\nolimits_{n \\geq 0} \\mathcal{E}_n$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{E}_0 = \\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\text{Sym}^n(\\mathcal{E}_1) \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{E}_n\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$n \\geq 0$", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "MATH_0010": "$S$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "MATH_0011": "$f : V \\to V'$", "MATH_0012": "$$\nf^* : \\pi'_*\\mathcal{O}_{V'} \\longrightarrow \\pi_*\\mathcal{O}_V\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-abstract-vector-bundle}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:a8346acb0c54bd92476c16ce8b7069c928d19cbc0ead6c0afd5dd91ac54fe260", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3033120f9b842777dad8d6b16f93080cdefa93a9cbd9fea46d6e4d9089aeef68", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d17dc0c12891fd581f3f2ac2fbb3672403e93334902a649c7b4518d6c55e59ed"}
